2. Wiring & Pin Connections
Power Rails: ESP32 5V Pin to Breadboard Positive (+) Rail; ESP32 GND Pin to Breadboard Negative (-) Rail.
MQ-2 Gas Sensor: VCC → 5V Rail | GND → GND Rail | A0 → ESP32 Pin GPIO 34
Flame Sensor: VCC → 5V Rail | GND → GND Rail | D0 → ESP32 Pin GPIO 35
DHT11 Sensor: VCC → 5V Rail | GND → GND Rail | DATA → ESP32 Pin GPIO 4
Active Buzzer: Positive (+) Pin → ESP32 Pin GPIO 19 | Negative (-) Pin → GND Rail
Relay Module: VCC → 5V Rail | GND → GND Rail | IN → ESP32 Pin GPIO 21
3. Step-by-Step Setup Guide
Set Up Firebase Cloud Database:
Go to Firebase Console (console.firebase.google.com) and create a new project.
Navigate to Build → Realtime Database → Create Database.
Select Start in Test Mode for easy reading/writing during testing.
Copy your Database URL (e.g., https://your-project-id.firebaseio.com/).
Upload Code to ESP32:
Open Arduino IDE on your computer.
Go to Tools → Library Manager, search for DHT sensor library by Adafruit, and click Install.
Paste the ESP32 source code below into your sketch. Replace YOUR_WIFI_NAME, YOUR_WIFI_PASSWORD, and YOUR_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID with your details.
Connect your ESP32 via USB and click Upload.
Launch Dashboard:
Copy the Web Dashboard code below and save it as index.html on your PC.
Replace YOUR_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID with your Firebase ID inside index.html.
Double-click index.html to open the live monitoring dashboard in any web browser.
